## Shopping

Most supermarkets have gluten free ranges. **Coeliac UK** has an app that lets you scan barcodes to check products.

## At home

- use a separate toaster or toaster bags
- use separate butter and spreads, or be careful not to use knives with crumbs
- clean surfaces before preparing gluten free food

## Eating out

Restaurants and cafes must be able to tell you if a dish contains gluten. Ask how food is prepared, and whether it could be contaminated.

## Travel

Take snacks, and look up gluten free options before you go. Coeliac UK has translation cards for travel abroad.

## Support

**Coeliac UK** has a helpline, recipes and local groups.
